    <sys:String x:Key="Msg_Content_InvalidFirstWord" xml:space="preserve">Line({0}) : {1}

The first word must be 'Alarm' or 'Timer'.

※ Correct format example
================
   Timer 12:30:00
   Alarm PM 02:22:12
================</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Msg_Content_TimerArgError" xml:space="preserve">Line({0}) : {1}

Timer requires time arguments and an optional memo.

※ Correct format example
================
   Timer 12:30:00
================</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Msg_Content_AlarmArgError" xml:space="preserve">Line({0}) : {1}

Alarm requires AM/PM, time, and an optional memo.

※ Correct format example
================
   Alarm PM 12:30:00
================</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Msg_Content_TimerFormatError" xml:space="preserve">Line{0} : {1}

Timer arguments must be 3 numbers separated by colons. 
 Ex) Timer 12:30:00</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Msg_Content_ParsingError" xml:space="preserve">(Line {0}) : {1}

The argument is not a valid number. 
 ※ Correct format example

================
   Timer 12:30:00
   Alarm PM 02:22:12
================</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Msg_Content_InvalidAmPm" xml:space="preserve">(Line {0}) : {1}

The first argument for Alarm must be AM or PM. 
 Ex) Alarm PM 12:30:00</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Msg_Content_AlarmFormatError" xml:space="preserve">Line{0} : {1}

Alarm's second argument must be 3 numbers separated by colons. 
 Ex) Timer 12:30:00</sys:String>

